{"id":"CVE-2002-0815","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2002-08-01T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T03:03:48.882Z","description":"The Javascript \"Same Origin Policy\" (SOP), as implemented in (1) Netscape, (2) Mozilla, and (3) Internet Explorer, allows a remote web server to access HTTP and SOAP/XML content from restricted sites by mapping the malicious server's parent DNS domain name to the restricted site, loading a page from the restricted site into one frame, and passing the information to the attacker-controlled frame, which is allowed because the document.domain of the two frames matches on the parent domain.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=102798282208686&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20020729 RE: XWT Foundation Advisory"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=102796732924658&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20020729 XWT Foundation Advisory: Firewall circumvention possible with all browsers"}],"vendors":["microsoft","mozilla"]}
