{"id":"CVE-2002-2436","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2011-12-07T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T04:06:54.689Z","description":"The Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) implementation in Mozilla Firefox before 4.0, Thunderbird before 3.3, and SeaMonkey before 2.1 does not properly handle the :visited pseudo-class, which allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information about visited web pages via a crafted HTML document, a related issue to CVE-2010-2264.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://blog.mozilla.com/security/2010/03/31/plugging-the-css-history-leak/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://w2spconf.com/2010/papers/p26.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=147777","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en/CSS/Privacy_and_the_:visited_selector","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/71816","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"firefox-css-info-disclosure(71816)"}],"vendors":["mozilla"]}
